From: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:52:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] tpm: Leave the self test to the TPM after starting it up

When the firmware has not started the TPM, tpm2_auto_startup() sees
TPM2_SelfTest refused with TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE, sends TPM2_Startup and
then sends TPM2_SelfTest again. With fullTest NO that asks the TPM to
test every algorithm it has not tested yet, which right after a
startup is all of them, and the probe waits for the answer.

A TPM tests an algorithm before its first use whether or not it was
asked to (TPM 2.0 Part 1, "Self-Test Modes"), so the second self test
only moves that work into the probe. Drop it. The startup's own
response code still says whether the TPM came up, and a TPM in failure
mode is still found by tpm2_get_cc_attrs_tbl(), whose TPM2_RC_FAILURE
sets TPM_CHIP_FLAG_FIRMWARE_UPGRADE as before. A TPM the firmware
started is tested by the first self test as before.

The self test is libtpms' longest command at boot: swtpm 0.10.2 took
25 ms to answer it on a laptop, and every other command of the probe
under 2 ms.
In a nested KVM guest with tpm-crb, the probe slept 18.5 ms on it
before PID 1 that a machine without a TPM does not.

"tpm: Start the tpm2 before running a self test" (2023-11) met the same
unstarted TPM and kept both self tests; the answer was that firmware
should start the TPM. Under qboot nothing does, and a firmware that did
would leave the kernel's first self test to pay instead.

Link: https://patchew.org/linux/20231122065528.1049819-1-hermin.anggawijaya@alliedtelesis.co.nz
Signed-off-by: Manuel de Brito Fontes <aledbf@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c b/drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c
index 4b2bb2d..949bac3 100644
--- a/drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c
+++ b/drivers/char/tpm/tpm2-cmd.c
@@ -723,14 +723,15 @@ int tpm2_auto_startup(struct tpm_chip *chip)
 	if (rc && rc != TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE)
 		goto out;
 
+	/*
+	 * A TPM tests each algorithm before its first use, so the self test
+	 * after a startup the kernel made would only move that work into the
+	 * probe.
+	 */
 	if (rc == TPM2_RC_INITIALIZE) {
 		rc = tpm2_startup(chip);
 		if (rc)
 			goto out;
-
-		rc = tpm2_do_selftest(chip);
-		if (rc)
-			goto out;
 	}
 
 	rc = tpm2_get_cc_attrs_tbl(chip);
-- 
2.53.0

